IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr5-sch3a`

-- TESTS for Schedule 3A (Excluded Trusts), lines 3082-3205.  Expected values are written from the text of each
-- paragraph before the run.  For each paragraph: a case that satisfies it (JUST TRUE), then each limb failed in
-- turn (NOTHING: the paragraph is one entry in a list that does not say "only"), then each boundary on both sides.
-- A definition given with "means" answers JUST FALSE outside it; paragraph 23A(2) ("does not apply") answers JUST FALSE.
-- Rulings of 2026-11-05: a "where" or "if" that is not met, a period the text fixes in its own words, and a case outside "only" each answer JUST FALSE; a case that fails only the description in
-- a paragraph with no trigger of its own stays NOTHING.


§ `sch 3A para 1 -- para 1 the trust is a legislative trust`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1 the trust is a legislative trust` WITH `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not imposed or required by an enactment: the paragraph does not say that such a trust is not excluded
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1 the trust is a legislative trust` WITH `the trust is imposed or required by an enactment` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 3A para 1+1 -- para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust und`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the day before the second anniversary of the death: less than two years has passed
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) the second anniversary itself: two years has passed, not less: outside the period the text fixes
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 1 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) after the second anniversary: outside the period
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 1 4 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) the day of the death: no time has passed
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 1 3 2024)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) before the death: no time has passed since it, so the period has not begun and the case is outside it
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 28 2 2024)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- leap-day death: 28 February 2026 is before the second anniversary (Date 29 2 2026 is 1 March 2026)
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 29 2 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- leap-day death: 1 March 2026 is the second anniversary under the Date convention: outside the period
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 29 2 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 1 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the trust has not ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1: the description is not met, and the paragraph does not say that another trust is not excluded
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS FALSE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a) the trust had not been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925: the "where" is not met
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS FALSE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS TRUE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) paragraph 1 ceased to apply for some reason other than the death of one of the trustees: the "where" is not met
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 1+1 the trust is a trust which ceases to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1 within two years of a trustee's death` WITH `the trust ceased to be an excluded trust under paragraph 1` IS TRUE, `the trust had been an excluded trust by virtue of section 34 of the Trustee Act 1925` IS TRUE, `the sole reason for paragraph 1 ceasing to apply is the death of one of the trustees` IS FALSE, `the date of the death of that trustee` IS (Date 1 3 2024), `the date for which the trust is being tested` IS (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `sch 3A para 2 -- para 2 the trust is a trust imposed by court order`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 2 the trust is a trust imposed by court order` WITH `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not created by or for a court or tribunal order
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 2 the trust is a trust imposed by court order` WITH `the trust was created by, or in order to satisfy the terms of, an order of a court or tribunal` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 3A para 3 -- para 3 the trust is a pension scheme trust`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 3 the trust is a pension scheme trust` WITH `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS TRUE, `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the pension scheme is not a registered pension scheme
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 3 the trust is a pension scheme trust` WITH `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS TRUE, `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the trust does not hold sums or assets of a pension scheme
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 3 the trust is a pension scheme trust` WITH `the trust holds sums or assets of a pension scheme` IS FALSE, `the pension scheme is a registered pension scheme for the purposes of Part 4 of the Finance Act 2004` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 3A para 4(1) -- para 4(1) the trust is a trust of a life policy paying out only on the`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(1) the trust is a trust of a life policy paying out only on the listed events or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of a life policy` IS TRUE, `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the life policy pays out in a case other than (a) or (b): the paragraph is closed by "only"
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(1) the trust is a trust of a life policy paying out only on the listed events or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of a life policy` IS TRUE, `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a trust of a life policy
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(1) the trust is a trust of a life policy paying out only on the listed events or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of a life policy` IS FALSE, `the life policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(1)(a) and (b)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 3A para 4(2) -- para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only `

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only on temporary disablement or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) temporary disablement but not applied for at the same time as a paragraph 4(1) policy: the "where" in (a) is not met, so the policy pays out in a case outside (a) and (b)
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only on temporary disablement or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS FALSE, `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) pays out only to meet healthcare costs: the 'same time' condition belongs to (a) only
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only on temporary disablement or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS FALSE, `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS FALSE, `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- pays out in a case outside (a) and (b): the paragraph is closed by "only"
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only on temporary disablement or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a trust of an insurance policy
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(2) the trust is a trust of an insurance policy paying out only on temporary disablement or for healthcare` WITH `the trust is of an insurance policy` IS FALSE, `the insurance policy pays out on the temporary disablement of the person assured` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy was applied for at the same time as a policy under paragraph 4(1)` IS TRUE, `the insurance policy pays out in a case outside paragraph 4(2)(a) and (b)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 3A para 4(3) -- para 4(3) the trust is a trust of the death benefits of a retirement p`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(3) the trust is a trust of the death benefits of a retirement policy` WITH `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a trust of the death benefits of a retirement policy
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 4(3) the trust is a trust of the death benefits of a retirement policy` WITH `the trust is of the benefits payable on the death of the person assured under a retirement policy` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 3A para 5 -- para 5 the trust is a charitable trust`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `Scotland`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS TRUE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) in Northern Ireland, registered
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `Northern Ireland`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS TRUE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) in Scotland, not registered
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `Scotland`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS FALSE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a) in Northern Ireland, not registered (the exemption in (b) is for England and Wales only)
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `Northern Ireland`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS FALSE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) in England and Wales, registered
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `England and Wales`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS TRUE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) in England and Wales, not required to register by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d)
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `England and Wales`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS FALSE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) in England and Wales, neither registered nor excused
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `England and Wales`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS FALSE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- in Scotland, not registered, but excused: the exemption is for England and Wales only
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS TRUE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `Scotland`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS FALSE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- not for charitable purposes
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 5 the trust is a charitable trust` WITH `the trust is for charitable purposes` IS FALSE, `the part of the United Kingdom in which the trust is` IS `Scotland`, `the trust is registered as a charity` IS TRUE, `the trust is not required to register as a charity by virtue of section 30(2)(a) to (d) of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `sch 3A para 6 -- para 6 the trust is a pilot trust`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 100, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) the value is exactly 100: 'not exceeding £100'
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 100, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) the value is 99
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 99, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) the value is 101
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 101, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) created the day before the date regulation 42(2)(iii) comes into force
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 100, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 31 12 2020), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) created on the date regulation 42(2)(iii) comes into force: not 'before', so outside the date the text fixes (read like a period: assumed, FORK S3A-F3)
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 100, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 1 1 2021), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) created after that date
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 100, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 2 1 2021), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) fails and (b) fails too: the date decides, whatever the value
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6 the trust is a pilot trust` WITH `the value of the property the trust holds` IS 101, `the date the trust was created` IS (Date 2 1 2021), `the date on which regulation 42(2)(iii) of these Regulations comes into force` IS (Date 1 1 2021)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `sch 3A para 6A(2) -- para 6A(2) the person is an authorised Part 4A person`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the person is an authorised Part 4A person` WITH `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 'means': an authorised person without the Part 4A permission is not an authorised Part 4A person
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the person is an authorised Part 4A person` WITH `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 'means': a person with no authorisation
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the person is an authorised Part 4A person` WITH `the person is an authorised person` IS FALSE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- neither
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the person is an authorised Part 4A person` WITH `the person is an authorised person` IS FALSE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `sch 3A para 6A(2) -- para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account` WITH `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 'means': the account consists of more than a sum of money
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account` WITH `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS FALSE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 'means': the holder is not an authorised Part 4A person
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account` WITH `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS FALSE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 'means': the holder does not carry on that activity by way of business
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(2) the account is a relevant account` WITH `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `sch 3A para 6A(1) -- para 6A(1) the trust is created as a requirement of opening a relevant`

-- the case that satisfies the paragraph
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(1) the trust is created as a requirement of opening a relevant account for the sole benefit of a minor or an incapable person` WITH `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS TRUE, `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) the sole beneficiary is under 18
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(1) the trust is created as a requirement of opening a relevant account for the sole benefit of a minor or an incapable person` WITH `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS TRUE, `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) lacks capacity within section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(1) the trust is created as a requirement of opening a relevant account for the sole benefit of a minor or an incapable person` WITH `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS TRUE, `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) incapable within section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000
#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(1) the trust is created as a requirement of opening a relevant account for the sole benefit of a minor or an incapable person` WITH `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS TRUE, `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d) incapable by reason of mental disorder within Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986
