#ASSERT (`sch 3A para 6A(1) the trust is created as a requirement of opening a relevant account for the sole benefit of a minor or an incapable person` WITH `the trust was created as a requirement of opening a relevant account` IS TRUE, `the account consists only of a sum of money` IS TRUE, `the person is an authorised person` IS TRUE, `the person has a Part 4A permission to carry on the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the person carries on by way of business the activity specified in article 5 (accepting deposits) of the Regulated Activities Order 2001` IS TRUE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person under the age of 18` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who lacks capacity within the meaning of section 2 of the Mental Capacity Act 2005` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable within the meaning of section 1 of the Adults with Incapacity (Scotland) Act 2000` IS FALSE, `the trust is for the sole benefit of a person who is incapable of managing and administering the person's property and affairs by reason of mental disorder within the meaning of Article 3(1) of the Mental Health (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
