-- the list of answers, gathered: the first list is the paragraphs' answers, the second what they would be if every unknown answer were yes
#ASSERT `sch 3A the answers of the paragraphs, gathered` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING, JUST TRUE) (LIST NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3A the answers of the paragraphs, gathered` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING) (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3A the answers of the paragraphs, gathered` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING) (LIST JUST TRUE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3A the answers of the paragraphs, gathered` (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING) (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3A the answers of the paragraphs, gathered` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE) (LIST JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an unknown answer is read as yes; a known one is left alone
#ASSERT `sch 3A treat an unknown answer as yes` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 3A treat an unknown answer as yes` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 3A treat an unknown answer as yes` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE

